I commented on and closed #1136, and left the other 11 issues alone because this session did nothing on them.

#1136 is fixed (231758c5). I re-ran the commands on the built binary (in a temporary git repo with a temporary home directory) before posting:
• goal set --bogus, skill search --bogus, skill install --bogus and lint fix --bogus now refuse with "unknown flag" and exit 2. Nothing runs.
• goal verify --bogus cargo test is refused too. I found this one while probing: before the fix it saved --bogus cargo test as the goal's verify command.
• goal set -- --bogus still works: it saves --bogus as the goal and exits 0, so -- lets you pass a dash-word on purpose.
• None of the refused commands wrote a file.

The fix adds one table in src/verb_flags.rs that gives each verb-and-subcommand pair its own rule for words starting with -. The tests read that table, so a new row gets checked automatically. My comment on the issue lists the rules and the tests.

